// emissions_mint is a real, already-initialized SPL Mint minted in setup() (same technique as
// bank_mint above). lending_pool_setup_emissions and lending_pool_update_emissions_parameters
// both structurally deserialize it (`InterfaceAccount<'info, Mint>`) and both derive the SAME
// `emissions_auth`/`emissions_token_account` PDAs off `[bank.key(), emissions_mint.key()]`, so
// this binding is deliberately bare/unqualified -- one fixture-level instance serves both.
// emissions_mint = self.emissions_mint
// emissions_auth is a pure PDA authority (`/// CHECK: Asserted by PDA constraints`,
// configure_bank.rs:151-160 -- AccountInfo, never itself holds initialized data, only ever used
// as a `token::authority`/CPI signer) for the per-(bank, emissions_mint) emissions vault. Only
// lending_pool_setup_emissions has an account literally named `emissions_auth` (grepped every
// instructions/**/*.rs), so a bare binding is safe.
// emissions_auth = Pubkey::find_program_address(&[EMISSIONS_AUTH_SEED, bank.as_ref(), emissions_mint.as_ref()], &self.program_id).0
// emissions_token_account is the per-(bank, emissions_mint) emissions vault PDA. `init`-gated
// ONLY by lending_pool_setup_emissions itself (configure_bank.rs:162-174) --
// lending_pool_update_emissions_parameters references the SAME PDA as a plain `mut`
// (configure_bank.rs:268-277, no `init`), so this bare binding cannot conflict with any other
// instruction's own `init`: the ONLY init-gate on this exact account is the very instruction this
// binding exists to unblock, and computing its address here (rather than pre-minting it in
// SCOUT:SETUP-GLUE) leaves lending_pool_setup_emissions's own real `init` to create it live on a
// successful call -- exactly the mandatory-safety-check-compliant version of this fix.
// emissions_token_account = Pubkey::find_program_address(&[EMISSIONS_TOKEN_ACCOUNT_SEED, bank.as_ref(), emissions_mint.as_ref()], &self.program_id).0
// emissions_funding_account (role: unchecked, AccountInfo -- only validated structurally by the
// real SPL Token program during the transfer_checked CPI, same class as signer_token_account
// above) is a real SPL TokenAccount of emissions_mint minted in setup() with a u64::MAX balance,
// owned by self.payer (== delegate_emissions_admin, the CPI transfer authority both instructions
// sign with), so the real transfer never fails for insufficient funds. Bare/unqualified for the
// same reason as emissions_mint above (shared by both emissions instructions).
// emissions_funding_account = self.emissions_funding_account
// flags (lending_pool_setup_emissions's own arg, u64) is written into Bank.flags via
// override_emissions_flag(flags), which HARD-PANICS (a raw `assert!`, not a catchable
// MarginfiError -- state/bank.rs:761-764,776-778) unless `flags & EMISSION_FLAGS == flags`. A
// fully-fuzzed u64 would panic on all but 4 of 2^64 values, so almost every call would never
// reach any line after configure_bank.rs:97. No line inside this handler branches differently
// across the 4 valid values (0/1/2/3), so pinning to the max valid value (both emission flags
// active) is the smallest edit that deterministically reaches every remaining handler line --
// this trades away fuzzing `flags` itself (now fixed) in exchange for the rest of the handler
// executing on every call instead of a ~0% fraction of them. Instruction-qualified since this
// arg name is unique to this one instruction (grepped), but qualified anyway per convention for
// an arg-value override, matching the vote-bp-style example in the setup-glue guidance.

