// --- lending_account_borrow: point it at the shared borrowable scenario ----------------------
// NOTE ON PRECEDENCE: `parse_bindings` (the generator) builds a plain dict keyed by
// `<Instruction>.<name>`, so the LAST line for a key wins. The five entries below therefore
// OVERRIDE the earlier `LendingAccountBorrow.amount = 0` / bare `marginfi_account = ...` /
// bare `bank = ...` entries above without editing them (these regions are additive-only).
//
// Root cause they fix: the generated action bound `bank` to the shared `self.bank`, which
// `scout_valid_bank_config(10)` pins to `borrow_limit: 0` / `asset_weight_init: 0` /
// `asset_weight_maint: 0` / `risk_tier: Isolated`. A direct probe of the real instruction against
// that bank with FOUR different remaining_accounts values (empty, [bank], [tokenless_bank], both)
// failed identically with `BankLiabilityCapacityExceeded` (6027, state/bank.rs:342, "amt: 1.0
// borrow lim: 0.0"), so this was never a remaining-accounts problem -- the shared bank simply
// cannot be borrowed against, and collateral deposited into it is worth zero to the health check.
// Reconfiguring it is not an option (a dozen sibling instructions branch on exactly those bits --
// see `scout_valid_bank_config_opt()`'s doc comment), hence the separate scenario built once in
// SCOUT:SETUP-GLUE by `scout_setup_borrow_scenario` (SCOUT:EXTRA-ACTIONS).
//
// `amount` was hardcoded `0` by an earlier binding, which cannot borrow anything even against a
// healthy bank; SCOUT_BORROW_AMOUNT is a real, in-limits amount (see SCOUT:PRELUDE for the
// ~1e6-successive-calls sizing, i.e. this is not a one-shot).
// `remaining_accounts` is a first-class binding key (`_remaining_accounts_call`,
// the generator): the plain form appends each pubkey read-only + non-signer, which is
// exactly what RiskEngine wants. `self.borrow_remaining_accounts` (a disjoint struct field, so it
// coexists with the `&mut self.ctx` borrow the builder chain holds) is the two scenario banks
// pre-sorted descending, matching `sort_balances()`; both are Fixed-oracle so one slot each.
// LendingAccountBorrow.amount = SCOUT_BORROW_AMOUNT
// LendingAccountBorrow.marginfi_account = self.borrow_marginfi_account
// LendingAccountBorrow.bank = self.borrow_liab_bank
// LendingAccountBorrow.remaining_accounts = self.borrow_remaining_accounts.clone()

// --- lending_account_repay: reuse the SAME scenario, on a real (not byte-patched) liability ---
// Same last-line-wins precedence note as above: these OVERRIDE the earlier
// `LendingAccountRepay.repay_all = Some(false)` / `.marginfi_account = ...` / `.bank = ...`
// entries rather than editing them.
//
// The pre-existing bindings routed repay through `scout_create_lending_account_repay_bank_with_
// liability`, which mints a fresh bank + account per call and then BYTE-PATCHES a liability whose
// share count equals the fuzzed `amount`. Two problems, both measured with a direct probe:
//   1. It is not real program state -- the liability is written straight into the account/bank
//      buffers, so any invariant that cross-checks bank totals against balances is reasoning about
//      a hand-forged state rather than one marginfi produced.
//   2. It only appears to work. 22 of 25 pseudo-random u64 `amount`s failed, because repay
//      transfers exactly `amount` tokens out of `self.signer_token_account`; a single ~9e18 repay
//      drains that u64::MAX funding account and every LATER token-moving action in the sequence
//      (deposit, repay, liquidate) then fails with SPL `insufficient funds`. That is almost
//      certainly why the campaign recorded 0/1 for this action.
// Pinning `repay_all = Some(true)` makes the handler ignore `amount` entirely
// (repay.rs:76-82: the `repay_all` arm calls `repay_all()` and never reads `amount`), so an
// arbitrary fuzzed value can no longer drain anything -- and, critically, the generated method
// KEEPS its `amount: u64` parameter, so both existing callers of
// `action_lending_account_repay(..)` still compile unchanged. `scout_borrow_scenario_ensure_
// liability` re-creates the liability with a real borrow before each call, which is what makes two
// repays in a row both succeed (repay_all closes the balance). The partial-repay branch given up
// here is covered by `action_lending_account_repay_partial_borrow_scenario` (SCOUT:EXTRA-ACTIONS).
// LendingAccountRepay.repay_all = Some(true)
// LendingAccountRepay.marginfi_account = self.borrow_marginfi_account
// LendingAccountRepay.bank = match self.scout_borrow_scenario_ensure_liability() { Some(v) => v, None => return false }

// --- lending_pool_handle_bankruptcy: give RiskEngine the one remaining account it needs -------
// Measured before the fix, by calling the real instruction with the generated action's OWN
// account assembly and no remaining_accounts:
//   ok=false error_code=Some(6008)
//   log| Program log: Ran out of remaining accounts at 0
//   log| AnchorError thrown in programs/marginfi/src/state/marginfi_account.rs:198.
//        Error Code: InvalidBankAccount. Error Number: 6008. Error Message: Invalid Bank account.
// i.e. the accounts were fine all along -- handle_bankruptcy.rs:72 constructs
// `RiskEngine::new(&marginfi_account, ctx.remaining_accounts)` before anything else, and that
// walks the account's ACTIVE balances consuming `get_remaining_accounts_per_bank()` slots each.
// The synthetic bankrupt account `scout_prepare_lending_pool_handle_bankruptcy_accounts()` mints
// has exactly ONE active balance, on the Bank that same helper mints, and that Bank is
// `OracleSetup::Fixed`, for which `get_remaining_accounts_per_bank()` is 1 -- the bank pubkey
// alone, no oracle account (price.rs:350-360 in fact REQUIRES the oracle slice to be empty for
// Fixed). So the complete list is `vec![bank]`.
// `bank` is the generated action's own local, `let`-bound from that same helper above the builder
// chain (the generator emits `.remaining_accounts(..)` after `.accounts(..)`, where every account
// local is in scope -- see `action_lending_account_borrow` for the emitted shape), so this
// expression can never drift from the account actually passed in `.accounts(..)`.
// This is byte-for-byte the list `action_lending_pool_handle_bankruptcy_reachable`
// (SCOUT:EXTRA-ACTIONS) has been sending successfully since it was written; the ONLY thing the
// generated action was missing was the list itself, so no new setup, account or arg is needed.
// Repeatable: the helper re-mints its bank + bankrupt account at the same two fixed,
// instruction-scoped seeds on every call, so the ACCOUNT_DISABLED flag and
// `KilledByBankruptcy` operational_state the first success writes are overwritten before the
// second call sends -- proven twice-in-a-row by
// `scout_lending_pool_handle_bankruptcy_binding_round::handle_bankruptcy_generated_action_succeeds_twice_in_a_row`.
// LendingPoolHandleBankruptcy.remaining_accounts = vec![bank]

// --- lending_pool_pulse_bank_price_cache: point the keeper pulse at a Fixed-priced bank -------
// Measured before the fix, by calling the real instruction from one fixture against four
// candidate banks:
//   self.bank                 -> ok=false error_code=Some(6031)
//                                log| AnchorError occurred. Error Code: OracleNotSetup.
//                                     Error Number: 6031. Error Message: Oracle is not set.
//   borrow_liab_bank          -> ok=true
//   borrow_asset_bank         -> ok=true
//   pulse_health_healthy_bank -> ok=true
// Root cause: `scout_valid_bank_config(..)` leaves the shared `self.bank` on
// `OracleSetup::None`, and pulse_bank_price_cache.rs:15 goes straight into
// `OraclePriceFeedAdapter::try_from_bank(&bank, ctx.remaining_accounts, &clock)`, whose `None`
// arm is an unconditional `Err(MarginfiError::OracleNotSetup)` (price.rs:97). No argument and no
// extra account rescues that -- the bank simply has no oracle. Configuring one ON `self.bank` is
// not an option: a dozen sibling instructions branch on exactly those config bits (see
// [rationale condensed for delivery — full derivation in git history]
// `self.marginfi_group`, whose StakedSettings PDA is deliberately NEVER created (SCOUT:SETUP-GLUE
// runs the entire staked chain against a SECOND, dedicated `staked_group` exactly so
// `action_init_staked_settings`'s own `init` on `self.marginfi_group`'s PDA stays reachable). The
// probe confirmed that PDA is absent. `sol_pool`/`stake_pool` were also unresolved
// `scout_placeholder()`s and `bank` was `self.bank`, an already-initialized non-PDA bank.
//
// The four fixes, in the order the generator emits the account locals (IDL order:
// marginfi_group, staked_settings, fee_payer, bank_mint, sol_pool, stake_pool, bank, vaults...):
//   * marginfi_group/staked_settings -> the dedicated staked chain setup() already builds.
//   * bank_mint -> a FRESH lst_mint per call from `scout_prepare_add_bank_permissionless()`
//     (SCOUT:EXTRA-ACTIONS), which also parks the triple's stake_pool root in
//     `self.perm_stake_pool` for the two slots below. It degrades to `None` -> `return false`.
//   * sol_pool/stake_pool -> that same triple, so the oracle validation's own derivation
//     (`["mint"/"stake", stake_pool]` under SPL_SINGLE_POOL_ID, state/price.rs:694-703) matches.
//   * bank -> the real `[marginfi_group, bank_mint, bank_seed]` PDA (add_pool_permissionless.rs:
//     178-182) instead of `self.bank`; the six vault/authority PDAs already derive off the `bank`
//     local, so they follow automatically with no entry of their own.
// `remaining_accounts` is the first-class binding key (`_remaining_accounts_call`): this handler
// calls `bank.config.validate_oracle_setup(ctx.remaining_accounts, Some(lst_mint), Some(stake_
// pool), Some(sol_pool))` (add_pool_permissionless.rs:124-129), which wants exactly
// `[oracle, lst_mint, sol_pool]`. `self.staked_oracle` is a disjoint struct field, so it coexists
// with the `&mut self.ctx` borrow the builder chain holds (same shape as the
// `LendingAccountBorrow.remaining_accounts` entry above); `bank_mint`/`sol_pool` are the locals
// emitted above (Pubkey is Copy, so moving them into `.accounts(..)` does not consume them).
// ⚠️ Mandatory safety check: see `scout_prepare_add_bank_permissionless()`'s doc comment -- the
// per-call-unique lst_mint makes the `bank` PDA unique per call for ANY fuzzed `bank_seed`, so
// this never collides with setup()'s own staked_bank and never disables its own next call.
// --- marginfi_account_place_order: ride the borrow scenario's asset+liability pair ----------
// The order PDA is seeded on the SORTED hash of the bank keys (order.rs:558-563 via
// `keys_sha256_hash`, ix_utils.rs:206-210), which the generator reports as an unresolvable seed
// -- so both the seed and the two args have to be supplied here. `authority` is the borrower's
// authority, which is the payer, and `fee_payer` pays `order_init_flat_sol_fee` (zero, since
// setup mints the fee state with all three flat fees at 0).
// MarginfiAccountPlaceOrder.bank_keys = self.scout_order_bank_keys()
// MarginfiAccountPlaceOrder.trigger = self.scout_order_trigger()
// MarginfiAccountPlaceOrder.marginfi_account = self.scout_order_account()
// MarginfiAccountPlaceOrder.order = self.scout_order_address()

// The rest of the order lifecycle rides the same PDA. `close_order` is the authority's own
// close; `set_keeper_close_flags` clears the balance tags the order reserved, which is exactly
// what makes `keeper_close_order` -- permissionless, three accounts, no signer -- able to close
// somebody else's order (order.rs:169-210). Placing, un-tagging and letting a stranger close is a
// sequence worth having reachable in one action pool.
// MarginfiAccountCloseOrder.marginfi_account = self.scout_order_account()
// MarginfiAccountCloseOrder.order = self.scout_order_address()
// MarginfiAccountCloseOrder.fee_recipient = self.payer.pubkey()
// MarginfiAccountKeeperCloseOrder.marginfi_account = self.scout_order_account()
// MarginfiAccountKeeperCloseOrder.order = self.scout_order_address()
// MarginfiAccountKeeperCloseOrder.fee_recipient = self.payer.pubkey()
