// --- Flashloan bracket (compound action) sizing -------------------------------------------------
// `lending_account_end_flashloan` is only valid as the tail of a start_flashloan..end_flashloan
// BRACKET inside ONE transaction (flashloan.rs:68-124), so it can never succeed as a generated
// single-instruction action. `action_flashloan_bracket` (SCOUT:EXTRA-ACTIONS) builds the real
// bracket with a FUZZER-CHOSEN middle, which is where the interesting behaviour lives: while
// ACCOUNT_IN_FLASHLOAN is set, `RiskEngine::check_account_init_health` returns Ok(()) immediately
// (state/marginfi_account.rs:546-551), so borrow/withdraw inside the bracket skip the init health
// check entirely; `end_flashloan` unsets the flag and then re-runs that check for real
// (flashloan.rs:147-152), which is what must hold at the transaction boundary.
//
// The vault liquidity is deposited by a separate provider account so borrow/withdraw have real
// tokens to move. The bracket account's own seed deposit is deliberately SMALLER than the maximum
// fuzzer-chosen middle amount, so a borrow can exceed its own collateral and create a genuine
// liability inside the bracket -- exactly the state end_flashloan's health re-check exists to
// reject (and that a borrow+repay_all pair inside the same bracket is expected to clear).
//
// TWO banks are needed, not one: `BalanceDecreaseType::BorrowOnly`
// (state/marginfi_account.rs:1286-1291) rejects a borrow from a bank the account already holds
// ASSETS in (`OperationBorrowOnly`, 6021 -- observed directly on the one-bank version of this
// action), so the deposit/withdraw arms and the borrow/repay arms must target different banks.
// SCOUT_FLASHLOAN_SEED_BORROW opens a small liability on the borrow bank BEFORE the bracket so
// both balances are already active and end_flashloan's positional remaining-account list is
// stable; it is far below the seed deposit's initial-weighted value (100_000 * 0.8 = 80_000), so
// the pre-bracket account is healthy.
const SCOUT_FLASHLOAN_VAULT_LIQUIDITY: u64 = 100_000_000;
const SCOUT_FLASHLOAN_SEED_DEPOSIT: u64 = 100_000;
const SCOUT_FLASHLOAN_SEED_BORROW: u64 = 1_000;
const SCOUT_FLASHLOAN_MIDDLE_AMOUNT_MODULUS: u64 = 1_000_000;

// --- shared, permanently borrowable scenario for lending_account_borrow / _repay -------------
// Amounts for the one borrowable (collateral bank, liability bank, borrower) triple built once in
// SCOUT:SETUP-GLUE by `scout_setup_borrow_scenario` (SCOUT:EXTRA-ACTIONS). Sized so the generated
// `action_lending_account_borrow` can be picked by the fuzzer essentially without limit rather
// than a handful of times:
//   * collateral 1e12 units at a Fixed price of 10 with asset_weight_init 0.8 => 8e12 of
//     init-weighted borrowing power, against a liability priced at 1 with liability_weight_init 1
//     => ~8e6 successive borrows of SCOUT_BORROW_AMOUNT before the init health check bites;
//   * the liability bank's vault is seeded with 1e12 by a separate liquidity-provider account
//     => ~1e6 successive borrows before the vault runs dry.
// Both are far beyond any realistic campaign's selection count for one action, and both are real
// program-enforced ceilings (not harness ones), so hitting them is a legitimate failure, not a
// harness bug. All three amounts are drawn from `self.signer_token_account`, which setup() funds
// with u64::MAX, so the deposits below consume ~2e12 of 1.8e19 (0.00001%).
const SCOUT_BORROW_COLLATERAL_DEPOSIT_AMOUNT: u64 = 1_000_000_000_000;
const SCOUT_BORROW_LIQUIDITY_DEPOSIT_AMOUNT: u64 = 1_000_000_000_000;
const SCOUT_BORROW_AMOUNT: u64 = 1_000_000;
