// lineage can create (pool depth 100, at most one account minted per action); the predicate fails
// open if it is ever exceeded, so an undersized value costs coverage, never correctness.
const SCOUT_KNOWN_CAP: usize = 256;
// Ring capacity for P-0006's registry of banks created by a real add-bank INSTRUCTION during
// fuzzing. Same shape and the same reason as SCOUT_KNOWN_CAP (an action hook may only assign, so
// this cannot be a Vec). Wrapping is safe here in the opposite direction: a wrapped ring loses
// entries, which lowers the LOWER bound P-0006 asserts, so it costs coverage and never
// correctness.
const SCOUT_P06_BANK_CAP: usize = 128;
// Ring capacity for the per-property SUBJECT registries of P-0001 / P-0017 / P-0020 / P-0022 /
// P-0039. Same shape and the same reason as SCOUT_KNOWN_CAP: the registries are grown by
// success-gated action-hook regions and by the setup/extra-action code that mints the account, and
// a hook may only ASSIGN, so none of them can be a Vec.
//
// SIZING. An entry is written only where the harness CREATES a MarginfiAccount or a
// LiquidationRecord -- four sites in setup(), five generated instructions
// (marginfi_account_initialize, marginfi_account_initialize_pda, marginfi_account_init_liq_record,
// transfer_to_new_account, transfer_to_new_account_pda) and the extra-action helpers that mint
// one. Every other instruction merely NAMES an account that some earlier site already registered,
// so a registry grows with account creations along a lineage, not with actions. 96 is several
// times the number of accounts a lineage has been observed to mint, and is deliberately modest:
// each entry is 32 bytes and the stateful pool stores one fixture clone per novel state (~15k
// states in a 25s two-worker campaign), so every slot is paid for ~15,000 times over.
//
// WRAPPING. The five registries divide into two kinds and the wrap policy differs by kind, stated
// here once rather than repeated in each block:
//   * P-0001 aggregates a SUM over its registry. A wrapped ring silently drops accounts, so the
//     sum UNDER-counts and the property could fire on a phantom loss or gain. It therefore fails
//     open exactly as P-0002 does (`scout_known_next > SCOUT_KNOWN_CAP` => return).
//   * P-0017 / P-0020 / P-0022 / P-0039 judge each subject INDEPENDENTLY. A wrapped ring can only
//     drop subjects, never invent one, so every verdict it still reaches is as sound as before and
//     the only cost is a false negative. Skipping the whole evaluation on wrap would ADD false
//     negatives without removing any false positive, so those four keep judging what they retain.
const SCOUT_SUBJECT_CAP: usize = 96;
// Capacity of P-0013's registry of banks PROVEN to have had CLOSE_ENABLED_FLAG set. Same
// fixed-array-plus-cursor shape as SCOUT_P06_BANK_CAP and for the same reason (an action hook may
