    // its own `LendingAccountBorrow.amount = 0` SCOUT:BINDINGS entry pins amount to zero, and
    // `self.bank`'s config (scout_valid_bank_config, SCOUT:PRELUDE) starts with
    // protocol_origination_fee = 0. Changing either of those shared defaults in place would
    // durably change fee economics (or the always-zero borrow) for every OTHER action that
    // touches `self.bank`/the generated borrow action for the rest of a campaign -- the same
    // mandatory-safety-check concern documented on `withdraw_bank`/`tokenless_bank` above. This
    // uses a SECOND, dedicated Bank (`self.fee_bank`, minted with a nonzero origination fee and
    // a directly-funded vault in SCOUT:SETUP-GLUE) and a SECOND, dedicated MarginfiAccount
    // (`self.fee_borrow_marginfi_account`, pre-flagged ACCOUNT_IN_FLASHLOAN so
    // `RiskEngine::check_account_init_health` short-circuits to `Ok(())` without needing real
    // collateral -- state/marginfi_account.rs:548-550) instead. Both are brand-new, non-PDA
    // Keypair-backed accounts distinct from every other named field, so nothing here can
