            // (state/bank.rs:158,162,171), every writer but one adds a non-negative quantity, and
            // the one subtracter takes `min(outstanding, available_liquidity).int() <= outstanding`
            // (collect_bank_fees.rs:57,75,130). So a negative counter is unreachable for ANY bank,
            // including the one whose floors the harness fabricates (they are positive constants),
            // and this arm is live from a subject's very first evaluation.
            scout_check!(
                "P-0030",
                "fee-counters-are-never-negative",
                insurance >= fixed::types::I80F48::ZERO
                    && group >= fixed::types::I80F48::ZERO
                    && program >= fixed::types::I80F48::ZERO,
                "P-0030: bank {} holds a NEGATIVE outstanding-fee counter (insurance={} group={} \
                 program={}). `Bank::new` zeroes all three (state/bank.rs:158/162/171); every \
                 writer except one adds a quantity that cannot be negative (accrue_interest's \
                 three `checked_add`s are guarded `> ZERO` at state/bank.rs:515/524/532; \
                 liquidate.rs:388 adds `insurance_fund_fee.frac()` after the same fee has already \
                 survived `checked_to_num::<u64>()`; marginfi_account.rs:1073/1118 add \
                 floor/ceil dust); and the one subtracter takes \
                 `min(outstanding, available_liquidity).int()`, which is <= outstanding \
                 (collect_bank_fees.rs:57/75/130). A negative value means booked fees were \
                 destroyed and the next payout will compute its transfer from a nonsense number -- \
                 the most likely source is borrow.rs:174/183, whose `saturating_add` SUBTRACTS if \
                 `protocol_origination_fee` is negative, a sign no config validation ever checks \
                 (state/interest_rate.rs:53-62 constrains only the utilisation curve)",
                bank,
                insurance,
                group,
                program
            );

