    // Ok(I80F48::ZERO); }` -- it does NOT error. So on a bank with a zero asset share value every
    // deposit mints exactly zero shares while the tokens are really transferred into the liquidity
    // vault, and every existing depositor's claim (`asset_shares * asset_share_value`) is already
    // zero. The bank is an unrecoverable sink. `utils/general.rs:306-307` is the guard that is
    // supposed to prevent anyone reaching it: `if bank.config.operational_state ==
